-- 1. pb_submit_bounties --------------------------------------------------
update playbook_nodes
set
  subtitle = 'Brands burn tens of thousands per day. You only need a sliver.',
  doc_content = E'**Here''s the part nobody told you.**\n\nBrands on the Ad Bounty program spend tens of thousands of dollars per day.\n\nYou get 3.5% of every dollar your ads spend.\n\nSo to cover your EcomTalent subscription, you need around $3K in spend across your bounties. That''s about $100 back to you.\n\nBrands burn through $3K in literal minutes.\n\nOne ad that performs and you''re inside for free.\n\nStack two winners and the math gets stupid. Students in this community have made $1K+/month from a single ad the brand kept running because it kept making them money.\n\nThat''s the prize. Here''s how to capture it.\n\n## Step 1. Apply once. Enroll per brand.\n\nOpen Discord. Find #ad-bounty-info. Click the start link.\n\nFill out the application (you''ll need a Wise account so payouts get automated). Approval takes 24-48 hours.\n\nOnce you''re in, enroll in one brand whose product you''d actually buy. Pin the submission link they DM you. That''s where every ad for that brand goes.\n\n## Step 2. Study before you film.\n\nRead the brand brief twice before you write a single frame.\n\nWatch their last 10 ads. Skim the market research doc.\n\nMost students skip this and waste their first bounty. Don''t be that person.\n\n## Step 3. One angle. Three variations.\n\nSame ad body. Three different hooks.\n\nLets Meta find which opening lands. Three is the sweet spot. Not one. Not six.\n\n## Step 4. Submit and wait.\n\nAI runs technical + brand QA in about 5 minutes.\n\nIf it passes, the media-buying team launches it within 24-48 hours. The brand runs it with their own budget. You never pay for spend.\n\n## Step 5. Track and get paid.\n\nWatch your dashboard. Real-time spend, ROAS, revenue per ad.\n\nPaid every two weeks. Automated to Wise based on your share of spend.\n\n## ⚠ The rule that decides everything: evergreen ads only.\n\nThe real game is making ads that keep running for a year. Two years. Indefinitely.\n\nEvery month the ad survives, you keep getting paid for work you did once. That''s how this compounds.\n\nThree hard rules:\n\n1. **No sales. No "ending today." No Black Friday angles.** If you reference a window, the ad dies when the window closes.\n2. **No prices in the ad.** Brands change pricing. Your "$29.99" ad becomes inaccurate and gets shut off.\n3. **Talk to people who''ve never heard of this product.** Solve a problem they have. Don''t pitch a feature list.\n\nBreak these rules and your ad doesn''t get launched.\n\n## Five things that actually move the needle\n\n**An hour of brand study beats a day of editing.** The students who win are the ones who knew the brand better than the brand expected.\n\n**Quality over volume.** Two thoughtful bounties beat ten lazy ones.\n\n**If five ads don''t get spend, your angle is the problem.** Not your craft. Stop iterating on edits. Start iterating on hooks and audiences.\n\n**When you hit a winner, remake it five ways.** Different hook. Different format (static if it was video, voiceover if it was text-on-screen). Different sub-audience. One winner is the start, not the finish.\n\n**Don''t marry the first brand.** Stack bounties across three or four. That''s how the income actually compounds.\n\n## When your first ad lands\n\nOpen your dashboard. Study why it worked. The hook. The visual. The angle.\n\nThen iterate. The students earning the most are the ones who turn one winner into five.\n\nTwo or three bounties in, even before you''ve won, head to **Build your portfolio**. Every ad you''ve shipped is a portfolio piece you didn''t know you had.',
  updated_at = now()
where id = 'pb_submit_bounties';

-- 2. pb_build_portfolio --------------------------------------------------
update playbook_nodes
set
  subtitle = 'It''s a Google Drive folder. That''s it.',
  doc_content = E'**Don''t overthink this.**\n\nA portfolio is one thing. A place where someone can click a link and see examples of your work.\n\nNot a website. Not a Framer landing page with your brand colors and a "Hi, I''m..." hero section.\n\nKarlo''s rule: clear over clever, every time.\n\nPick whatever lets a brand click once and see your work. Google Drive folder works. Notion page works. One scrollable doc works.\n\nThe simplest one is the right one.\n\n## Your first move\n\nOpen a Google Drive folder right now.\n\nTitle it "Your Name - Ad Creative."\n\nDrop in every ad you made in the 30-day sprint. Action items, bounties, statics, organics, the ones that didn''t work. All of them.\n\nYou already have a portfolio. You just haven''t put it in a folder yet.\n\n## What goes in it\n\nThe work itself, and the truth about it. That''s the whole standard.\n\n1. **Every action item from the sprint.** UGC, organic, VSL, static, all of it. That''s why Karlo made you do them in this order. By the end of the sprint you have 10-20 ads to point at.\n2. **Every bounty you''ve submitted.** Even the ones that didn''t get spend yet. Submitted ads = real ads for real brands.\n3. **For winning bounties: the numbers.** Spend, ROAS, revenue. Pull them off your bounty dashboard and write them next to the ad. "This ad generated $X for [brand]" beats anything else you could say.\n4. **Group by format.** UGC in one section, statics in another, VSLs in another. Lets a brand spot what they need in 10 seconds.\n\n## ⚠ What NOT to do\n\n**Don''t rip other people''s work.** It''s everywhere right now and brands know it. That''s why most job posts ask for an editing trial. Be the person who doesn''t need to fake it.\n\n**Don''t wait for a "good enough" piece before you start.** That''s the move that kills 90% of portfolios. Your first version exists today.\n\n**Don''t build a fancy website.** You''re not a designer pitching designers. Brands want to click a link and see ads. Spend the time making more ads instead.\n\n**Don''t be precious about it.** Action items count. Bounties without spend count. Free trials count. The portfolio is where the work lives, not a museum of your wins.\n\n## How to actually apply with it\n\nThis is where the folder pays off.\n\n**Text application?** Drop the link. Don''t write a wall of copy explaining what you can do. Brands judge in 30 seconds whether they want to talk to you.\n\n**Loom application?** This is the differentiator.\n\nA 2-3 minute Loom over the brand''s job post. "Here''s what you posted, here''s what I''d do, here''s my work."\n\nThat''s what got Karlo most of his clients. Everyone applies with text. Almost nobody records a Loom. That''s the gap you walk through.\n\n**If they ask for an editing trial, do it.** Free. Two hours of effort. Treat it like a bounty. Two hours of free work has landed students retainers worth thousands per month because the brand kept them long-term.\n\n## When you''re ready\n\nThe moment you have a folder with anything in it (even three action items and one bounty), head to **Apply to the job board.**\n\nThe folder is a tool. Applying is the move that actually changes your income.',
  updated_at = now()
where id = 'pb_build_portfolio';

-- 3. pb_apply_job_board --------------------------------------------------
update playbook_nodes
set
  subtitle = 'Karlo posts new brand opportunities almost every day.',
  doc_content = E'**One client changes you.**\n\nThe job board has new brands posting almost every day. They''re looking for the exact thing you just spent 30 days getting good at.\n\nEditing video ads. Writing static ads. Building UGC.\n\nEditing for one real brand teaches you ten times faster than studying. The path from "I''m learning" to "I''m a marketer" runs through this card.\n\n## Your first move\n\nOpen the job board. Scan the latest five posts.\n\nApply to the one that excites you. Not the one that pays the most.\n\nDo it before you close this sheet.\n\n## How to apply\n\n1. **Read the brand''s brief.** Watch their last three ads. Notice what''s working and what''s missing.\n2. **Send a short application.** Two sentences: who you are, why this brand. Drop your portfolio link. That''s it.\n3. **If they ask for a sample**, make ONE ad to spec. Free. Treat it like a bounty.\n4. **Track every reply.** Even the no''s. Patterns show up after three or four applications.\n\n## Five things that get you replies\n\n**Apply to brands you actually want to work with.** Mediocre fit = mediocre work.\n\n**Quality over volume.** Five thoughtful applications beat thirty templates.\n\n**Mention specifics from their brief.** Generic outreach gets ignored.\n\n**A "no" today often becomes a "yes" in three weeks.** Stay friendly. Keep shipping.\n\n**Set a daily 5-minute window** to check the board. Karlo posts almost every day. Don''t miss them.\n\n## ⚠ The Loom move\n\nThis is what separates the top 1% of applicants from the rest.\n\nRecord a 2-3 minute Loom over the brand''s job post. Walk through what they posted. Tell them what you''d do. Show them one piece of relevant work.\n\nThat''s it.\n\nEveryone applies with a wall of text. Almost nobody records a Loom. The Loom is what got Karlo most of his clients in the early days.\n\nIf you only do one thing on this card, do this.\n\n## When you''re ready\n\nWhen a brand says "send me a sample," that''s the moment.\n\nThe next card is the one that matters most.',
  updated_at = now()
where id = 'pb_apply_job_board';

-- 4. pb_land_first_client ------------------------------------------------
update playbook_nodes
set
  subtitle = 'The line between learning and earning. You only cross it once.',
  doc_content = E'**This is the line.**\n\nOn one side: someone learning a skill.\n\nOn the other: someone paid for it.\n\nThe first client changes how you see yourself. Not just what''s in your account.\n\nIt''s the moment the whole 30-day sprint stops being theory.\n\n## Why this card matters more than the other three\n\nKarlo says it in almost every part of the program: once you land the first one, everything starts to change.\n\nThe skill compounds. The next clients come faster. The rate goes up.\n\nBut the first one is the one you remember.\n\n## How you get there\n\nThis card doesn''t have a tutorial.\n\nThe path runs through the three cards before it. Bounty after bounty. Portfolio piece after portfolio piece. Application after application.\n\nShow up. Send the work. Don''t blink when it takes longer than you wanted.\n\n## What "landing a client" actually looks like\n\nIt''s almost never glamorous.\n\nUsually it''s a Loom reply, then a Discord DM, then a Stripe link.\n\nSometimes it''s a $200 first project. Sometimes it''s a $3K/month retainer. Both count. Both cross the line.\n\nThe size of the first deal doesn''t matter. What matters is the proof that someone, somewhere, paid you for the skill you''ve been building.\n\n## When it happens\n\nPress the button below.\n\nThe celebration is real because the moment is real.\n\nThe work continues. But you''ve already crossed.',
  updated_at = now()
where id = 'pb_land_first_client';

